|	I think a shopkeeper will only accept money after you've angered him
|if the reason was because you stole something of value.  I guess he values
|his life as "priceless".

That is fair but as the shop keepers are there to make money, and they
can identify anything (to set the price), I think they should be able
to do more than just stand there.

What I'd like to see is that you can go up to them and `chat' to get a
list extra things.

for example
#chat to shop keeper (screen is over writen)

Shop Keeper Prestego : Food Shop on Level 7
You owe Prestego 130 gold pieces
(M) Map Level       100 gp
(I) Identify Item   200 gp
(R) Remove Curse    500 gp
(B) Recharge Item  1000 gp
(W) Wish           9000 gp
(Q) Quit talking to Prestego


The above is only a posible example of the charges and abilities that
shop keepers of future dungeons may offer. It would also be very easy
to implement.

  The only comment I'd make is that the cost of the things offered should
be reasonably higher than the price of an equivelent magic item.
The prices should also vary occording to charisma and hawian shirt.
and could variy with the status of the player in relation to shop keepers
EG is the keeper angry, has the player killed a pervious shop keeper,
Has the player robbed a shop (via kicking/teleporting or doggy training)

